<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-July 14.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-July 14.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended July 14</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     355	   1.61     640050  227.22   23.65</p>
<p>Telco		  440	   2.01     239600  105.42   23.82</p>
<p>TISCO		  215	   0.95     477750  102.72   23.04</p>
<p>Castrol		620	   2.73     102800   63.74   22.96</p>
<p>STERLITE	     225	   1.08     206200   46.40   25.03</p>
<p>Colgate		315	   1.47     141300   44.51   24.33</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   895	   4.14	41300   36.96   24.12</p>
<p>BHEL		   390	   1.84	91000   35.49   24.60</p>
<p>Tata Power	   137	   0.63     234950   32.19   23.98</p>
<p>Atlas Copco	  280	   1.45     112000   31.36   27.00</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 29.37 percent on an annualised basis against 27.50 percent in the previous carry forward account ended June 05.</p>
<p>Note :- BC - Book Closure</p>
